Recall the tangent sum formula: $\tan(A + B) = \frac{\tan A + \tan B}{1 - \tan A \tan B}$.  Applying this to our terms, we get
\begin{align*}
\frac{\sin(A+B)}{\cos(A+B) }
&= \frac{\frac{a}{b+c} + \frac{b}{a+c}}{1 - \frac{ab}{(b+c)(a+c)}} \\
&= \frac{ac + b^2 + a^2 + bc}{bc + c(a+b) - ab} \text{.}
\end{align*}, <answer>$\frac{\pi}{4}$</answer>

